  "tier_merge": {
    "applied": true,
    "why": "The native 3-way split is even by size and tops the domain on macro-silhouette, but its 2nd- and 3rd-healthiest clusters are not materially different in insurance coverage (0.046 IQR separation on life_coverage_ratio, 0.064 on ci_coverage_ratio; CI inverts on the mean, life on density). The real structure is 'adequately covered' vs 'not'. Merging keeps the validated winner's actual partition rather than switching to a k=2 model \u2014 no k=2 candidate reproduces this 33.7/66.3 split, and the one flagged alternative (B|gmm_full|2) fails the project's own 5% normal-population floor at 3.4%.",
